From: PicoW-usb2bt-hfp <dev@example.com>
Subject: [PATCH] bta_ag_sco: log SCO TX write status (debug only)

Optional bring-up aid: print the result of BTM_WriteScoData() and the
current SCO state for every outgoing SCO packet.  This is noisy and runs
at ERROR level, so apply it only when debugging the SCO/HCI TX path.

---
 components/bt/host/bluedroid/bta/hf_ag/bta_ag_sco.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/components/bt/host/bluedroid/bta/hf_ag/bta_ag_sco.c b/components/bt/host/bluedroid/bta/hf_ag/bta_ag_sco.c
--- a/components/bt/host/bluedroid/bta/hf_ag/bta_ag_sco.c
+++ b/components/bt/host/bluedroid/bta/hf_ag/bta_ag_sco.c
@@ -873,6 +873,7 @@ static void bta_ag_sco_event(tBTA_AG_SCB *p_scb, UINT8 event)
             if (len_to_send == p_scb->out_pkt_len) {
                 if (p_sco->state == BTA_AG_SCO_OPEN_ST) {
                     tBTM_STATUS write_stat = BTM_WriteScoData(p_sco->p_curr_scb->sco_idx, p_buf);
+                    APPL_TRACE_ERROR("SCO TX write_stat=%d len=%u state=%d", write_stat, len_to_send, p_sco->state);
                     if (write_stat != BTM_SUCCESS) {
                         break;
                     }
